>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SLOW_BEST_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.SLOW_BEST_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by less committing best-first classical search.

`SLOW_BEST_TAC thms` safely saturates the whole state, then expands the
first goal. Its frontier uses the total normalized size of all open goals.
The tactic uses the slow cascade:
unsafe-rule alternatives remain available after instantiating alternatives
have been found. Children are enumerated eagerly, and no dynamic per-goal
pruning is performed. `clasetSearch.node_limit` defaults to 100000
expanded states; setting it to a non-positive value disables the limit.

The theorem list locally accepts `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`,
`SDest`, `Dest` and `Del` markers. Unmarked theorems become unsafe
introduction rules. Generic simplifier markers such as `Cong`, `Excl` and
`SF` do not become classical rules.

The tactic succeeds only with a replayed proof that closes every goal.

### Failure

Fails if the frontier is exhausted or the node limit is reached before a
complete proof is found. Marker processing can also reject malformed extra
rules.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem slow_best_tac_example:
  (p \/ q) ==> (p ==> r) ==> (q ==> r) ==> r
Proof
  classicalLib.SLOW_BEST_TAC []
QED
```

